.Sh DESCRIPTION
CMS_signerInfo contains separate attribute lists for signed and unsigned
attributes.
Each
.Xr CMS_signed_XXX 3
function is used for signed attributes, and each
.Xr CMS_unsigned_XXX 3
function is used for unsigned attributes.
Since the
.Xr CMS_unsigned_XXX 3
functions work in the same way as the
.Xr CMS_signed_XXX 3
equivalents, only the
.Xr CMS_signed_XXX 3
functions are described below.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_by_OBJ
finds the location of the first matching object
.Fa obj
in the SignerInfo's
.Fa si
signed attribute list.
The search starts at the position after
.Fa lastpos .
If the returned value is positive then it can be used on the next call
to
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_by_OBJ
as the value of
.Fa lastpos
in order to iterate through the remaining attributes.
.Fa lastpos
can be set to any negative value on the first call, in order to start
searching from the start of the signed attribute list.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_by_NID
is similar to
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_by_OBJ
except that it passes the numerical identifier (NID)
.Fa nid
associated with the object.
See <openssl/obj_mac.h> for a list of NID_*.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr
returns the
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
object at index
.Fa loc
in the
.Fa si
signed attribute list.
.Fa loc
should be in the range from 0 to
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_count
- 1.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_delete_attr
removes the
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
object at index
.Fa loc
in the
.Fa si
signed attribute list.
An error occurs if the
.Fa si
attribute list is NULL.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr
pushes a copy of the passed in
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
object to the
.Fa si
signed attribute list.
A new signed attribute list is created if required.
An error occurs if
.Fa attr
is NULL.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_OBJ
creates a new signed
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
using
.Xr X509_ATTRIBUTE_set1_object 3
and
.Xr X509_ATTRIBUTE_set1_data 3
to assign a new
.Fa obj
with type
.Fa type
and data
.Fa bytes
of length
.Fa len
and then pushes it to the
.Em key
object's attribute list.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_NID
is similar to
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_OBJ
except that it passes the numerical identifier (NID)
.Fa nid
associated with the object.
See <openssl/obj_mac.h> for a list of NID_*.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_txt
is similar to
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_OBJ
except that it passes a name
.Fa attrname
associated with the object.
See <openssl/obj_mac.h> for a list of SN_* names.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get0_data_by_OBJ
finds the first attribute in a
.Fa si
signed attributes list that matches the
.Fa obj
starting at index
.Fa lastpos
and returns the data retrieved from the found attributes first
.Sy ASN1_TYPE
object.
An error will occur if the attribute type
.Fa type
does not match the type of the
.Sy ASN1_TYPE
object OR if
.Fa type
is either
.Sy V_ASN1_BOOLEAN
or
.Sy V_ASN1_NULL
OR the attribute is not found.
If
.Fa lastpos
is less than -1 then an error will occur if there are multiple objects
in the signed attribute list that match
.Fa obj .
If
.Fa lastpos
is less than -2 then an error will occur if there is more than one
.Sy ASN1_TYPE
object in the found signed attribute.
.Pp
Refer to
.Xr X509_ATTRIBUTE 3
for information related to attributes.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Xr CMS_unsigned_XXX 3
functions return values are similar to those of the equivalent
.Xr CMS_signed_XXX 3
functions.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_count
returns the number of signed attributes in the SignerInfo
.Fa si ,
or -1 if the signed attribute list is NULL.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_by_OBJ
returns -1 if either the signed attribute list of
.Fa si
is empty OR if
.Fa obj
is not found, otherwise it returns the location of the
.Fa obj
in the SignerInfo's
.Fa si
signed attribute list.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_by_NID
is similar to
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr_by_OBJ
except that it returns -2 if the
.Fa nid
is not known by OpenSSL.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get_attr
returns either a signed
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_delete_attr
returns either the removed signed
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
or NULL if there is a error.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr ,
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_OBJ ,
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_NID ,
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_txt ,
return 1 on success or 0 on error.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_get0_data_by_OBJ
returns the data retrieved from the found signed attributes first
.Sy ASN1_TYPE
object, or NULL if an error occurs.
.Sh NOTES
Some attributes are added automatically during the signing process.
.Pp
Calling
.Xr CMS_SignerInfo_sign 3
adds the NID_pkcs9_signingTime signed attribute.
.Pp
Calling
.Xr CMS_final 3 ,
.Xr CMS_final_digest 3
or
.Xr CMS_dataFinal 3
adds the NID_pkcs9_messageDigest signed attribute.
.Pp
The NID_pkcs9_contentType signed attribute is always added if the
NID_pkcs9_signingTime attribute is added.
.Pp
Calling
.Xr CMS_sign_ex 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign_receipt 3
or
.Xr CMS_add1_signer 3
may add attributes depending on the flags parameter.
See
.Xr CMS_add1_signer 3
for more information.
.Pp
OpenSSL applies special rules for the following attribute NIDs:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It CMS Signed Attributes
NID_pkcs9_contentType NID_pkcs9_messageDigest NID_pkcs9_signingTime
.It ESS Signed Attributes
NID_id_smime_aa_signingCertificate NID_id_smime_aa_signingCertificateV2
NID_id_smime_aa_receiptRequest
.It CMS Unsigned Attributes
NID_pkcs9_countersignature
.El
.Pp
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr ,
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_OBJ ,
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_NID ,
.Fn CMS_signed_add1_attr_by_txt
and the equivalent
.Xr CMS_unsigned_add1_attrXXX 3
functions allow duplicate attributes to be added.
The attribute rules are not checked during these function calls, and are
deferred until the sign or verify process (i.e.
during calls to any of
.Xr CMS_sign_ex 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign_receipt 3 ,
.Xr CMS_add1_signer 3 ,
.Xr CMS_Final 3 ,
.Xr CMS_dataFinal 3 ,
.Xr CMS_final_digest 3 ,
.Xr CMS_verify 3 ,
.Xr CMS_verify_receipt 3
or
.Xr CMS_SignedData_verify 3 ) .
.Pp
For CMS attribute rules see RFC 5652 Section 11. For ESS attribute rules
see RFC 2634 Section 1.3.4 and RFC 5035 Section 5.4.
